The inductive invariant is that evaluating every symbolic
stack entry in any legal environment gives exactly the concrete
stack after the instruction prefix. This proves soundness
for accepted inputs under the specified instruction semantics.
Structural equality is not complete for arithmetic equivalence:
the validator rejects a constant-folded candidate for $8-2$
even though it correctly pushes $6$. Supporting such cases
would require an additional verified rewrite rule or a richer
equivalence check, not weaker stack validation.
